ition:** INDEPENDENT\n**Automated operational score:** 95/100 — LOW — APPROVE\n*This tool is for demonstration purposes only.*\n\n### Summary\nThe AI reviewer reported 1 confirmed actionable finding(s).\n\n### Findings\n- **LOW · SECURITY_VULNERABILITY · SSH allow rule applies to all subnet destinations rather than a specific target resource**\n  - Category rationale: The AllowSSH rule (priority 300) permits TCP port 22 inbound from a single approved source address (203.0.113.10/32). While this is a significant improvement over an open rule, 203.0.113.10/32 is a single public IP address with no further restriction on destination addresses within the subnet (destination_address_prefix = '*'). Any resource in the associated subnet is reachable on port 22 from this source. If multiple VMs or resources exist in the subnet now or in future, this expands the SSH attack surface beyond a single intended target. More critically, the destination_address_prefix of '*' means the rule applies to all hosts in the subnet rather than a specific management IP, which is a concrete over-permissioning of the SSH allow rule as configured.\n  - Evidence: azurerm_network_security_group.nsg, security_rule 'AllowSSH': source_address_prefix = '203.0.113.10/32', destination_port_range = '22', destination_address_prefix = '*', priority = 300, direction = 'Inbound', access = 'Allow'.\n  - Analysis: The AllowSSH security rule in azurerm_network_security_group.nsg sets destination_address_prefix = '*', permitting the approved source (203.0.113.10/32) to reach TCP port 22 on any resource within the associated subnet (subnet-demo, 10.0.1.0/24). This is broader than necessary if the intent is to restrict SSH to a specific management host. Any current or future resource added to the subnet is automatically covered by this allow rule without requiring an explicit change.\n  - Impact: All resources in subnet 10.0.1.0/24 are reachable on SSH port 22 from the approved source address. If additional VMs or services are deployed into this subnet, they inherit SSH exposure without any additional rule change, increasing the lateral movement and attack surface risk within the research environment.\n  - Recommendation: Restrict destination_address_prefix to the specific IP address or prefix of the intended SSH management target (e.g., a specific VM private IP) rather than '*'. If the subnet is intended to host only one SSH-accessible resource, document this explicitly and consider tightening the destination when that resource's IP is known.\n\n### Recommendation\nReview and remediate the confirmed findings above.\n","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/abdulwaheed384/ai-pr-review/issues/comments/6147872303/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":{"id":15368,"client_id":"Iv1.05c79e9ad1f6bdfa","slug":"github-actions","node_id":"MDM6QXBwMTUzNjg=","owner":{"login":"github","id":9919,"node_id":"MDEyOk9yZ2FuaXphdGlvbjk5MTk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9919?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/github","html_url":"https://github.com/github","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github/received_events","type":"Organization","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"name":"GitHub Actions","description":"Automate your workflow from idea to production","ext